            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous aortic valvuloplasty as a bridge to a high-risk percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E238-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a novel approach of using percutaneous aortic valvuloplasty as a bridge to percutaneous coronary intervention in a patient with refractory congestive heart failure, severe aortic stenosis, severe left ventricular dysfunction and severe 3-vessel coronary artery disease who was not a surgical candidate for aortic valve replacement and coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
